Ladybird now shapes text that a system fallback font draws with the
element’s font features, as it shapes text in the element’s own
fonts. In Chrome 157 and Firefox 151, Armenian text set in Times New
Roman (which has no Armenian, so a system font draws it) lost its
ligature under a font-feature-settings that turned liga off, and
under “font-variant-ligatures: none”. Ladybird kept the ligature in
both cases before this change.

From their source: Blink’s HarfBuzzShaper takes the features from Font::
GetFontFeatures(), which the element’s FontDescription decides for every
font of the run, fallback fonts included. And Gecko’s gfxFontShaper::
MergeFontFeatures() reads them from the text run’s gfxFontStyle, which
applies to whichever font its gfxFontGroup falls back to.
